      "question": "Given that a single shorten call can't both keep the XML body at exactly 500 chars-including-fence AND feed the colored path's independently-shortened Edit diff, how do you want to resolve the unification?",
      "header": "Approach",
      "multiSelect": false,
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "Encapsulate, keep output (Recommended)",
          "description": "Keep the three representations but move the three-way shorten into one cohesive operation on ToolParts (e.g. ToolParts.shorten(width)), co-located with the type. Each renderer still formats on its own terms; every current byte (XML/raw/colored/JSON) is preserved; the 'forgot to shorten one copy' bug-class is structurally closed. Smallest safe diff, but it doesn't literally 'shorten once' \u2014 it makes the all-three-together invariant impossible to forget."
        },
        {
          "label": "Normalize, relax 500-incl-fence",
          "description": "Drop the denormalized `content` field; ToolParts carries one raw structured payload that each renderer derives its view from; shorten the payload literally once. Truly achieves 'shorten once' and is arguably more correct (the 500 budget covers the payload, not payload+fence). Cost: XML --short bytes shift, so test_short_modifier.py's exact-500 assertions get updated to expect payload-500. Intentionally changes observable --short output."
        },
        {
          "label": "Skip \u2014 already fixed",
          "description": "The recent commit (56d47c2) already closed the real leak, and the three-way shorten now lives in a single block in model.py. The remaining bug-class (someone adds a 4th representation and forgets it) is speculative. Per YAGNI, leave it as is."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
